THE MOS 6502 · node 6502 · 6502 · THE MOS 6502 · exereunesis · chip teardown · 1975 · UD0 / exereunesis

universe of origin : the teardown — a made machine, opened and explored
seal               : The 6502 is the most consequential cheap chip in computing history. At about a quarter the price of its rivals, this tiny 8-bit processor powered the Apple II, the Commodore 64, the Atari machines, the BBC Micro — and, in derived form, the NES. It put computers and consoles in millions of homes.
